response:
 If yes, then prove it by writing out 4283 as the sum of successive integers:


\begin{aligned} n &= { 4283 \over 1 }\\ &= 4282 + 1 \end{aligned}

For demonstration purposes, I changed the integer 4283 to 4282 by multiplying it by the multiplicative inverse of 2 modulo 10. By the way, the decimal values 0.35 and 0.86 are not real numbers because they are not integer fractions.
